  "primer": {
    "$comment": "Zenburn palette for gen-primer-theme. Source: https://github.com/jnurmine/Zenburn colors/zenburn.vim, which declares GNU GPL in its header and has no LICENSE file — colour values only, no code reused. Values: Normal bg #3f3f3f (#1f1f1f for the high-contrast option), fg #dcdccc, CursorColumn #4f4f4f, Visual #2f2f2f, LineNr/Directory #9fafaf, Comment #7f9f7f, Constant #dca3a3, String #cc9393, Error-ish #e37170, Function #efef8f, Keyword #f0dfaf, Number #8cd0d3, cyan #93e0e3, magenta #dc8cc3 / #ec93d3, orange #dfaf8f, green #88b090 / #709080, Title #efefef, StatusLine #ccdc90. Base: @primer/primitives dark. Zenburn is deliberately low-contrast: canvas #3f3f3f, inset/shadow #2b2b2b and #232323 derived, raised #4f4f4f, borders #5f5f5f/#6f6f6f derived. Text fg, muted #9fafaf (4.6:1; the comment green is 3.6:1 -> disabled), accent + primary button + link #8cd0d3 (dark text), success #7f9f7f for backgrounds with text lifted to #9bb195 (4.6:1), danger #dca3a3 (#e37170 for emphasis bgs), attention #f0dfaf, severe #dfaf8f, done + sponsors #dc8cc3 with text #ec93d3 (4.9:1).",
    "neutral_chroma_max": 0.025,
    "dark_tint_max_L": 0.4,
    "shadow_color": "#232323",
    "chroma_boost": 1,
    "hue_ranges": [
